"warren prime — agent session context (v0.14.0)\n\nCommands:\n  add-project — register a project on the warren server (POST /projects)\n      --default-branch <name>  override the auto-detected default branch\n      --url <url>  warren server base URL (env WARREN_BASE_URL)\n      --token <token>  bearer token (env WARREN_API_TOKEN)\n  run — dispatch a one-shot run against the warren server, tail events as NDJSON, and exit\n      -p, --prompt <text>  prompt text the agent receives\n      --trigger <label>  run trigger label\n      --provider <name>  per-run override of agent frontmatter.provider\n      --model <name>  per-run override of agent frontmatter.model\n      --max-cost-usd <usd>  per-run USD spend cap; wins over the agent's own and the project default\n      --url <url>  warren server base URL (env WARREN_BASE_URL)\n      --token <token>  bearer token (env WARREN_API_TOKEN)\n  init — scaffold a .warren/ directory (triggers.yaml + config.yaml) in a project repo\n      --project <id>  target a registered project by id (writes into its warren clone)\n      --cwd <path>  target a directory on disk (defaults to process.cwd())\n      --default-role <name>  pin defaults.defaultRole to this registered agent\n      --url <url>  warren server base URL (env WARREN_BASE_URL)\n      --token <token>  bearer token (env WARREN_API_TOKEN)\n  config — .warren/ admin tools\n  config migrate — convert legacy .warren/defaults.json into the warren-5840 YAML layout (config.yaml + preview.yaml)\n      --project <id>  target a registered project by id (writes into its warren clone)\n      --cwd <path>  target a directory on disk (defaults to process.cwd())\n      --url <url>  warren server base URL (env WARREN_BASE_URL)\n      --token <token>  bearer token (env WARREN_API_TOKEN)\n  doctor — check the client's view of a warren server (reachable? auth valid? version match?)\n      --local  run the deployment-side checks instead (env vars, burrow socket, bwrap, DB)\n      --no-auth  skip the auth check (loopback dev mode)\n      --verbose  print raw probe/driver output (withheld from check messages) to stderr\n      --url <url>  warren server base URL (env WARREN_BASE_URL)\n      --token <token>  bearer token (env WARREN_API_TOKEN)\n  db — database admin tools\n  db migrate-to-postgres — one-shot copy of a SQLite warren.db into a Postgres database\n      --from <sqlite>  source SQLite path or URL (bare path, sqlite://, file://, :memory:)\n      --to <pg-url>  target Postgres URL (postgres:// or postgresql://)\n  plan — dispatch and steer cloud plan-runs\n  plan run — dispatch a serial plan-run against a remote warren and tail events as NDJSON\n      --project <id>  project id (prj_xxx)\n      --agent <name>  registered agent name\n      --prompt-template <text>  per-child prompt template override\n      --ref <git-ref>  git ref to clone child workspaces from\n      --provider <name>  per-run override of agent frontmatter.provider\n      --model <name>  per-run override of agent frontmatter.model\n      --max-cost-usd <usd>  per-child USD spend cap applied to every child dispatch\n      --no-follow  dispatch and exit without tailing events\n      --output <mode>  output mode: ndjson (default) or pretty\n      --url <url>  warren server base URL (env WARREN_BASE_URL)\n      --token <token>  bearer token (env WARREN_API_TOKEN)\n  plan cancel — cancel a remote plan-run and its in-flight child run\n      --output <mode>  output mode: ndjson (default) or pretty\n      --url <url>  warren server base URL (env WARREN_BASE_URL)\n      --token <token>  bearer token (env WARREN_API_TOKEN)\n  plan status — render a plan-run's child-state table with per-child cost + duration\n      --output <mode>  output mode: ndjson (default) or pretty\n      --url <url>  warren server base URL (env WARREN_BASE_URL)\n      --token <token>  bearer token (env WARREN_API_TOKEN)\n  plan list — list plan-runs, optionally filtered by project / state\n      --project <id>  only plan-runs for this project (prj_xxx)\n      --state <state>  only plan-runs in this state (queued|running|succeeded|failed|cancelled)\n      --output <mode>  output mode: ndjson (default) or pretty\n      --url <url>  warren server base URL (env WARREN_BASE_URL)\n      --token <token>  bearer token (env WARREN_API_TOKEN)\n  show — render a run's detail (GET /runs/:id; json mode is the raw run document)\n      --url <url>  warren server base URL (env WARREN_BASE_URL)\n      --token <token>  bearer token (env WARREN_API_TOKEN)\n  wait — poll a run to its terminal state (SDK waitForRun; exit 0 on succeeded)\n      --timeout <seconds>  overall wait budget in seconds (default 1800)\n      --url <url>  warren server base URL (env WARREN_BASE_URL)\n      --token <token>  bearer token (env WARREN_API_TOKEN)\n  tail — stream a run's events (GET /runs/:id/events; SIGINT detaches, exit 130)\n      --no-follow  drain the current backlog and exit instead of following\n      --from-seq <n>  replay only events after this seq\n      --url <url>  warren server base URL (env WARREN_BASE_URL)\n      --token <token>  bearer token (env WARREN_API_TOKEN)\n  cancel — cancel a non-terminal run (POST /runs/:id/cancel; idempotent)\n      --reason <text>  operator note recorded on the cancel\n      --url <url>  warren server base URL (env WARREN_BASE_URL)\n      --token <token>  bearer token (env WARREN_API_TOKEN)\n  login — verify a base URL + token against the server and persist them to the client config\n      --url <url>  warren server base URL (env WARREN_BASE_URL)\n      --token <token>  bearer token (env WARREN_API_TOKEN)\n  prime — emit agent session context: command reference, env contract, exit codes, workflows\n  serve — start the HTTP server (default in docker entrypoint)\n      --no-auth  boot without bearer-token auth (loopback only)\n\nEnvironment:\n  WARREN_BASE_URL — warren server base URL (default http://localhost:8080)\n  WARREN_API_TOKEN — bearer token for the server (required unless WARREN_AUTH=public)\n  WARREN_CLIENT_CONFIG — override the client config path (default ~/.warren/client.json, written by `warren login`)\n\nExit codes:\n  0  success — the command completed successfully\n  1  run-failed — the dispatched run/plan-run reached a non-success terminal state, or the command failed for any other reason\n  2  usage-error — bad flags or arguments (missing required option, invalid --output value, validation error)\n  3  server-unreachable — the warren server did not answer the pre-flight probe\n  4  auth-rejected — the server rejected the bearer token (HTTP 401/403)\n  130  sigint-detach — operator detached a live event tail with SIGINT; the remote run keeps going\n\nWorkflows:\n  dispatch-and-wait:\n    warren login --url <base> --token <t>   # once; stores credentials in the client config\n    warren run <agent> <project-id> -p \"<prompt>\"   # dispatch, tail NDJSON events, exit with the terminal state\n  tail-and-steer:\n    warren run <agent> <project-id> -p \"<prompt>\"   # each NDJSON line is one event\n    Ctrl-C detaches the tail (exit 130); the remote run keeps going\n  plan-run:\n    warren plan run <plan-id> --project <id> --agent <name>   # serial children, each gated on the previous PR merging\n    warren plan status <plan-run-id>   # child-state table with per-child cost + duration\n    warren plan cancel <plan-run-id>   # cancel the plan-run and its in-flight child"
